  data: {
    LLM: "1. Standard Trick Play: The trump caller leads the first trick. Players must follow suit if possible.\n2. The Consecutive Rule: Tricks are NOT picked up after each round. They remain face down in a pile in the center of the table.\n3. Capturing: To pick up the pile of tricks, the same player (not just the same team) must win TWO consecutive tricks. When that happens, that player's team collects the entire centre pile.\n4. Reset: Once the tricks are collected, the pile in the center is empty. The winner of the last trick leads the next.",
    Player: "1. Standard Trick Play: The trump caller leads the first trick. Players must follow suit if possible.\n2. The Consecutive Rule: Tricks are NOT picked up after each round. They remain face down in a pile in the center of the table.\n3. Capturing: To pick up the pile of tricks, the same player (not just the same team) must win TWO consecutive tricks. When that happens, that player's team collects the entire centre pile.\n4. Reset: Once the tricks are collected, the pile in the center is empty. The winner of the last trick leads the next.",
    objective: 'Capture as many tricks as possible. The team that wins at least 7 of the 13 tricks wins the round.',
    gameplay: "1. Standard Trick Play: The trump caller leads the first trick. Players must follow suit if possible.\n2. The Consecutive Rule: Tricks are NOT picked up after each round. They remain face down in a pile in the center of the table.\n3. Capturing: To pick up the pile of tricks, the same player (not just the same team) must win TWO consecutive tricks. When that happens, that player's team collects the entire centre pile.\n4. Reset: Once the tricks are collected, the pile in the center is empty. The winner of the last trick leads the next.",
    keyRules: [
      'The 13th trick is always collected by the winner of that trick, along with any remaining cards in the center pile.',
      'Only the same player (not the partner) winning two consecutive tricks may collect the centre pile.',
      'If tricks 1-12 are not collected (no one wins two in a row), the winner of the 13th trick takes the entire board (very rare).',
